    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SqafgoSjp92zUDvJ2Nde6X)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #454, #457, #460 and #461 (all merged); no dependency on open PRs.\n- Touches `sp-fetch-inbox.el` (item listing and the picker). Another thread (filing inbox PDFs) and #470 may edit the same file; hunks are kept small, so the likely result is a small textual conflict, not a behaviour change.\n- Merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n\n## What it does\n\n- Picker of `sp-fetch-inbox` can be sorted:\n  - `added`: newest first (DEVONthink addition date, or file modification time in `inbox/`); this is the default\n  - `alphabetical`: by name, ignoring case\n  - `sp-fetch-inbox-sort` sets the default; `C-c s` in the picker switches (typed input is kept)\n- Picker is grouped by the sub-directories that exist in `inbox/` (`sp-fetch-inbox-group`, default on):\n  - files directly in `inbox/` are in `(inbox)`\n  - DEVONthink sub-groups of the `inbox` group are listed too, as folders of the same name\n- Restrict to one folder: `C-c d` in the picker, or `C-u M-x sp-fetch-inbox` before it.\n- Vertico/Consult/default UI keep the order: completion metadata sets `display-sort-function`, `cycle-sort-function` and `group-function`.\n- Keys are shown in the picker prompt, not the echo area: the echo area is the minibuffer while picking, so `sp-echo-help` hints are suppressed there.\n- Duplicate names get the folder appended so each candidate is unique.\n- Literate doc updated (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-fetch-inbox.org`, new section \"The picker\"); the `.el` is the tangled output (checked identical).\n\n## Tested\n\n- 25 ERT tests pass in Emacs 29.3 (`tests/sp-fetch-inbox-test.el`): parsing, folder/time detection, both orders, grouping, unique candidates, completion metadata, sort/folder switching logic.\n- Byte-compiles with no new warnings.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- The real minibuffer (Vertico grouping headings, `C-c s` / `C-c d` key bindings, restart of the picker) was not run: no GUI Emacs or completion UI in the container.\n- DEVONthink JXA (sub-group walk with `r.type() === \"group\"`, `additionDate()`) could not run here; if sub-groups are not detected, their records are just missing from the picker (as before).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `M-x sp-fetch-inbox` with files in `inbox/` and in a sub-folder: candidates are grouped, newest first\n- [ ] `C-c s`: order switches to A-Z and back; the text typed so far stays\n- [ ] Vertico/Consult does not re-sort the candidates (order matches the prompt)\n- [ ] `C-c d` lists the folders with counts; choosing one shows only that folder; \"All folders\" restores\n- [x] `C-u M-x sp-fetch-inbox` asks for the folder first\n- [ ] Customize `sp-fetch-inbox-sort` to `alphabetical`: picker starts A-Z\n- [ ] A DEVONthink sub-group of `inbox` appears as its own group; record order follows the DEVONthink addition date\n- [ ] Two files with the same name in different folders are both selectable\n- [ ] Filing an article still works end to end (C-c C-c)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCUww3znLZuUxrn6jW)_",
